# Dual remotes — youjune (origin) is the source of truth

When the user asks to commit and/or push this repo:

- Remotes: `origin` = `https://github.com/youjune2005/umbrella.git` (**canonical**), `sewon` = `https://github.com/sewon202/umbrella.git` (**mirror only**).
- `origin` / youjune always wins. Treat `origin/main` as the real history. `sewon` is updated to match it, not the other way around.
- After a successful local commit, push **`origin` first**, then `sewon`, unless the user explicitly asks for only one.
- Keep `main` tracking `origin/main` only. Never set upstream to `sewon`.
- If `sewon` and `origin` diverge, prefer `origin`. Do not reset or rewrite local/`origin` to match `sewon`. To sync the mirror, push `origin`'s branch to `sewon` (ask before `--force` / `--force-with-lease` on `sewon`).
- Do not commit `umbrella.db`.
- Still follow authorship rules: Youjune Park only; never Cursor `Co-authored-by`.
